Ideas only, no code: huntharo/git (PwrGit's git fork, GPL-2.0) and the upstream
git "worktree add --reflink" patch (GPL-2.0). From their design documents we took
the re-fstat of the donor after cloning, FIDEDUPERANGE re-sharing with a FIEMAP
"already shared" check, and the list of edge cases. No GPL code was copied.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
josharian/git-cow-worktree  (https://github.com/josharian/git-cow-worktree, read at commit 0f6852c)

Ported to Rust: the v2 index writer (src/index.rs, from index.go), the add flow
(--no-checkout, clone, verify, seeded index, `checkout -f HEAD`, retry on a
rejected index, post-checkout via `git hook run`; src/add.rs, from main.go,
clone.go, validate.go, seed.go, tree.go, worktree.go), and the shape of the
drop-in invariant test scenarios (tests/dropin.rs, from e2e_test.go).

